# RUN 2 of 4. Provenance, stated plainly: this run PREDATES the --anonymise flag, so its
# session ids were replaced here post-hoc by sha256 prefix. It was NOT produced by the
# published code -- samples/bench_cache_residency.out is the run that was. Token counts
# and timings are untouched.
#
# Kept because arm 5 is the headline claim and one run is not a reproduction.
ARM 1 -- RESIDENT: one process, two turns over stream-json stdin
  resident turn1: cache_read=26220 cache_creation=0 input=2875
  resident turn2: cache_read=15566 cache_creation=14268 input=1083

ARM 2 -- FRESH: turn 1 in one process, turn 2 in a NEW process via --resume
  fresh turn1: {'sid': 'sid-e80bbc34', 'read': 26220, 'create': 0, 'inp': 2863}
  fresh turn2 (new process, resumed, inside TTL): {'sid': 'sid-e80bbc34', 'read': 26220, 'create': 2892, 'inp': 164}

ARM 3 -- SUFFIX PERTURBATION (kept, and it FAILED as a control)
  perturbed turn2: {'sid': 'sid-e80bbc34', 'read': 14848, 'create': 14483, 'inp': 2}

ARM 4 -- PREFIX PERTURBATION, the real control: switch model to 'haiku' (caches are keyed per model)
  model-switched turn2: {'sid': 'sid-e80bbc34', 'read': 30993, 'create': 130, 'inp': 10}

ARM 5 -- DEAD-WRITER TEST: does a cache written by an EXITED process get read by a new one?
  A (writer; exits before B and C run): {'sid': 'sid-94b5710c', 'read': 14848, 'create': 11416, 'inp': 2863}
  B (new process, SAME marker as the dead writer):      {'sid': 'sid-94b5710c', 'read': 26264, 'create': 2875, 'inp': 164}
  C (new process, DIFFERENT marker -- the control):     {'sid': 'sid-94b5710c', 'read': 14848, 'create': 14464, 'inp': 2}

READING
  resident 2nd-turn cache_read=15566   fresh 2nd-turn cache_read=26220
  NOT like-for-like: the resident arm's turn 2 follows a longer cached prefix. Do not quote this pair as residency being cheaper.
  suffix-perturbed cache_read=14848 vs unperturbed 26220  <- did NOT drop; either way this arm is NOT a reliable control (--append-system-prompt is a SUFFIX change)
  model-switched hit_frac=100% (read=30993 creation=130) vs unperturbed hit_frac=90% (read=26220 creation=2892)
    PRIMARY (hit-fraction) -> control FAILED
    SUPERSEDED (read-ratio) -> control FAILED  [kept visible: this is the test that misread a 4.9x creation increase as no-miss]

VERDICT
  THIS RUN PROVES NOTHING. Arm 4 did not show a miss, so the instrument was not shown to discriminate a hit from a miss on this run -- and a run in which nothing COULD have missed cannot evidence that nothing DID.
